{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense","id":1326765,"title":"[Aberrant] Super-Speed Defense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-22T11:56:44-07:00","id":1326765,"title":"[Aberrant] Super-Speed Defense","content":"So, I just noticed that if you make a super-speedster (ala, Flash or Quicksilver) they are just as easily hit as any other person. I think this is a small hole in the game's super-hero emulation.<br /> <br /> I'll put this in my official feedback, but I had a couple of ideas that could sure up this issue without breaking the core of the game. <br /> <br /> 1st idea: A two or three-point Edge that allows a character to roll the lower of their Cunning or Dexterity when making a Defense roll.<br /> <br /> 2nd idea: A Mega-Edge that has the prerequisite of Mega-Dexterity that increases your Defense Scale by your dots in Mega Dexterity. <br /> <br /> The Mega-Edge is important because it emulates the unearthly reaction time and precision of a super-speedster. If a modification needed to make for the second one, it could be along the lines of idea one and have the scale only increase by the lower of the character's mega-dexterity or mega-cunning. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T12:36:15-07:00","id":1326775,"title":"","content":"I like the Pretercognition mega-edge. It's simple and effective. If you want to power it up a bit more, maybe allow spending a point of Quantum to make the increase cost to Inflict Damage on the nova equal to their Mega-Dex or Mega-Cunning scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T13:03:13-07:00","id":1326782,"title":"","content":"Oh it is good. It helps with a certain flavor of superhero. Just don't work for what I am seeing as a difficency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T13:12:48-07:00","id":1326784,"title":"","content":"In core it was a bit of mental shift in that Storypath Dexterity isn't a 1:1 to old Storyteller Dexterity, and that some of the capabilities we attribute (snicker) to Dex are shared among the Resilience Traits, although I would like to see more support for Dex in Edges or Skill Tricks. Even the &quot;Precise Martial Arts&quot; Edges can use Close Combat instead of Dex, so it seems to have little impact on one's hand to hand combat abilities.<br /> <br /> That gets a bit strained when Super Speed comes into play.<br /> <br /> I don't think it should be a straight Scale Application, and should probably require quantum like the Mega-Dex Attack Edge does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T13:14:04-07:00","id":1326785,"title":"","content":"The speedster himself get a enhancement on his defence when running equals to his speed scale.<br /> <br /> I will sugest a edge to add to defence, like Mega-Dodge or something, 1 to 5 dots limited to his Mega Dexterity dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T14:29:30-07:00","id":1326802,"title":"","content":"Mateus, Where is the speedster getting the bonus to defense from running? Did I miss something in the rules?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T14:30:34-07:00","id":1326805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326782#post1326782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh it is good. It helps with a certain flavor of superhero. Just don't work for what I am seeing as a difficency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly Mega dexterity does not have anything to do with speed. it is being supernaturally agile, not quick. You want to do it something it explicitly isnt.<br /> <br /> What you see as deficiency is also superhero staple. Speedsters are not immune to being hit at all and often are significantly more prone to it. This simulates traditional superhero genre perfectly.<br /> <br /> All of your solutions have same issue. They make game mostly unplayable Giving free scale without limit to defense is a bad idea. Being megas they are inherent and thus cannot be countered, are cheap and do not have meintenance and lack counter unlike powers, which are explicitly counterable. Easy acess to defensive scale, without counter and with other benefits creates the same trap as exalted perfects. Battle must be shaped accordingly and perfect trap is present.<br /> <br /> Fot it to work. It must Be power and never edge, so you can pull limits and disrupton in easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T14:42:28-07:00","id":1326811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326802#post1326802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mateus, Where is the speedster getting the bonus to defense from running? Did I miss something in the rules?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>When they talk about scale they are not just talking about size and durability, but also scale, and it\u2019s said more than once that scale can impact on defence and even make impossible to hit the target at all.<br /> <br /> On Trinity they didn\u2019t put it in details, but its implied that the higher scale grant some scale enhancements on defence. More than once devs have commented that it work as described in Scion, where the defence gains 1 enhancement per scale.<br /> <br /> Notice that it apply just when the guy is running, not when he is standing and avoiding to be hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:08:52-07:00","id":1326813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326784#post1326784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the &quot;Precise Martial Arts&quot; Edges can use Close Combat instead of Dex...</div> </div> </div> </div>I goofed. It is CC AND Dex for the Precise Martial Arts Edges, so there is a precedent for Edges allowing Dex to contribute to Defense.<br /> <br /> So we have some precedent, and then there is the Mega-Edge Rapid Strike that boosts Attacks, so I think there is a case for it. But it shouldn't be Scale, or at least 1 to 1 Scale. MMight giving combat scale always on for no cost is kinda warping. Still working through how that shakes down, and also really makes me question if MStam is supposed to actually work as defensive Scale, or if that was a holdover in the MMight entry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:18:58-07:00","id":1326815,"title":"","content":"My original idea would be that the mega-edge just adds 1e per Mega-Dex dot to Defense Rolls. <br /> <br /> I can see Defensive Scale getting so big as to not be able to hit a character. Which is frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:19:33-07:00","id":1326816,"title":"","content":"The idea of using Cunning to increase the defence is not bad. Actually is as good as Dexterity, dodging is as much detecting the attack as it is taking the body out of the way.<br /> <br /> But I still prefere the reverse of Accuracy in the defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:22:04-07:00","id":1326818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326815#post1326815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My original idea would be that the mega-edge just adds 1e per Mega-Dex dot to Defense Rolls. <br /> <br /> I can see Defensive Scale getting so big as to not be able to hit a character. Which is frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agility (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Mega-Dexterity or Mega-Cunning equal to dots<br /> The nova\u2019s grace and speed from Mega-Dexterity applies to avoid being hit as well. For each dot in Agility, the nova gains 1 Enhancement on defensive rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:23:37-07:00","id":1326819,"title":"","content":"Yup, that is basically what I wanted to create. I think it would be a solid edition with getting the idea of a super-speedster across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T15:57:40-07:00","id":1326824,"title":"","content":"My thought on this (nothing official, just trying to conceptualize) is that you roll for Defense when attacked. You roll a resistance trait (Composure, Stamina, Resolve) and add it to your base Defense of 1 (assuming you are using it all to purchase the Dodge Stunt). At super speed (meaning you've bought the Mega-Speed Edge, not that you have Mega-Dexterity), you are literally attempting to dodge the attack. I could definitely see your SG giving your Speed Scale as an advantage to that roll to add Enhancement as long as you use that Enhancement for the Dodge Stunt. That would then really depend on what you're dodging. A swung sword is likely only Speed Scale 1, meaning you are going to start adding Enhancement at Speed Scale 2 and just dodge the shit out of it at Speed Scale 4 or higher. A speeding bullet is more likely Speed Scale 5 (based on a quick google search and comparing it to say a fighter jet), which means that to dodge that sucker, you're going to need to have at least Speed Scale 6 to even start adding Enhancement to your roll for being faster than the bullet.<br /> <br /> That said, another way to think about how speedsters just aren't there to be hit is in Range Bands. A speedster can move 2 Range Bands for every 1 someone without a Speed Scale bump can. So you can outdistance your opponent who is trying to punch you without even breaking a sweat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T16:10:28-07:00","id":1326827,"title":"","content":"Makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> This is one thing scales do to the game, they apply almost every time, but every once in a while the lower scale attacker can avoid the scale difference using some tactics, hitting a soft spot of a big target, hitting the speedster while he cans dodge, things like that.<br /> That\u2019s a good reason to not have a fixed rule as Scale always add 1 to defence.<br /> <br /> The idea of dodging bullets requiring higher scale I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s a requirement. The guy aiming is not as fast as the bullet, so if you are aware of the guy shooting you could sidestep just in time, not requiring outrun the bullet.<br /> If you have no space to sidestep and need to outrun it, than you must be fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T06:33:57-07:00","id":1326948,"title":"","content":"One thing Impernious didn\u2019t add, and make sense not adding, is a Mega-Edge as the Agility we made.<br /> <br /> Mega-Speed is enough to do the effect, you are that fast, not just because you move your legs, but because you can react super fast. In this case, the \u201crunning to get enhancement\u201d should be eliminated completely.<br /> <br /> A Psion flying at speed 6 is fast, but he can\u2019t dodge bullets, he just is accelerating really fast in one direction, same for a Jet Fighter, but a Speedster need to react super fast to do their trick, as they can run between people and dodge buildings coming at speed 6 in their directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T06:54:49-07:00","id":1326949,"title":"","content":"I am confused by what you are saying. that we do need an agility mega-edge, or that we don't and Mega-Speed handles it? If it is the latter, how does Mega-Speed help you with Defense?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T07:03:49-07:00","id":1326951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326949#post1326949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused by what you are saying. that we do need an agility mega-edge, or that we don't and Mega-Speed handles it? If it is the latter, how does Mega-Speed help you with Defense?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We don\u2019t need another Mega-Edge, Mega-Speed gives the character enough reaction time to avoid being hit.<br /> <br /> Mega-Speed is not just about flying super fast or running super fast, it\u2019s about reacting super fast too, for example they can run super fast between cars, and stop immediately if need, not like a vehicle.<br /> <br /> The Agility MEdge can be just for Mega-Cunning Novas, reacting to the slightest suggestion of attack. Mega Speed is about moving out of the way mid atttack and Agility is about reacting to avoid the attack from the moment it started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-23-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T07:16:57-07:00","id":1326956,"title":"","content":"Ok, now I see what you mean. This is why clarification on all these Scales and their implications need to be the rule book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T10:30:24-07:00","id":1327005,"title":"","content":"RAW, you would need some careful applications of your increased movement and cover. Kind of a hitch in a turn based system that if you use your extreme movement and are in the open between turns you are functionally standing still when someone else has their turn, even if on your turns you were running at Super-sonic speed. Could probably stand to be a special use case under the current super-speed edge, or an additional MEdge. I'm thinking instead of just adding enhancement or scale or soft armor it would be neat to add a Complication to attacks equal to Speed Scale. Flexes a different part of the system, and could potentially dovetail nicely into Mega-Dex's use case of cancelling Complications. Or maybe if you have been moving a certain number of rangebands a turn you effectively have various levels of cover.<br /> <br /> The specified rolls and usage are there for a reason, and there is an overarching principle of the rules being flexible, but if you are constantly having to bend the rules for something, there should probably just be a change to the rules.<br /> <br /> I could also see this being an opportunity to use marvels, I mean Power Stunts, but again, if you keep finding yourself having to make the same exception over and over again you probably need a new rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 07-23-2019, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T11:09:23-07:00","id":1327017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327005#post1327005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW, you would need some careful applications of your increased movement and cover. Kind of a hitch in a turn based system that if you use your extreme movement and are in the open between turns you are functionally standing still when someone else has their turn, even if on your turns you were running at Super-sonic speed. Could probably stand to be a special use case under the current super-speed edge, or an additional MEdge. I'm thinking instead of just adding enhancement or scale or soft armor it would be neat to add a Complication to attacks equal to Speed Scale. Flexes a different part of the system, and could potentially dovetail nicely into Mega-Dex's use case of cancelling Complications. Or maybe if you have been moving a certain number of rangebands a turn you effectively have various levels of cover.<br /> <br /> The specified rolls and usage are there for a reason, and there is an overarching principle of the rules being flexible, but if you are constantly having to bend the rules for something, there should probably just be a change to the rules.<br /> <br /> I could also see this being an opportunity to use marvels Power Stunts, but again, if you keep finding yourself having to make the same exception over and over again you probably need a new rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your ideas of adding complications related to the target scale, makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> The problem is we are used to the rules telling what to add to the target defence and when, but the scale may or may not be used according to the situation, and that is where the flexible rules apply or not, up to the SG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T15:19:12-07:00","id":1327081,"title":"","content":"Steve answered my question about the scale difficulties, it\u2019s +2 difficulty per scale on any action against a higher scale.<br /> <br /> The Mega-Fast Nova gains +2 on defence per scale difference of the scale apply.<br /> <br /> So, if Spider-Man have a Mega-Speed 1 he can move around the city as fast as a car (faster because the traffic) and can dodge most of the attacks (+2 in defence), that\u2019s fair for our neighbourhood friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:25:54-07:00","id":1327104,"title":"","content":"Now my only big issue with Scales is that Leadership Scale get two way of increasing it (mega-presence and mega-manipulation) but mega-Composure does not directly counter nor is their another Scale that counters Leadership. Making Social Nova very potent. Now.....I could see Leadership Countering Leadership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:36:01-07:00","id":1327111,"title":"","content":"Danielle just answers that. Leadership counter Leadership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:56:52-07:00","id":1327112,"title":"","content":"Yup. I read that after I posted. Good Stuff.<br /> <br /> Not sure how I feel about that, specifically that it means that the best way to counter-mental abilities it just grabbing more Mega-Presence and Manipulation. However, once I do more thinking on it, that discussion may be better for another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T20:47:08-07:00","id":1327126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327081#post1327081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steve answered my question about the scale difficulties, it\u2019s +2 difficulty per scale on any action against a higher scale.<br /> <br /> The Mega-Fast Nova gains +2 on defence per scale difference of the scale apply.<br /> <br /> So, if Spider-Man have a Mega-Speed 1 he can move around the city as fast as a car (faster because the traffic) and can dodge most of the attacks (+2 in defence), that\u2019s fair for our neighbourhood friend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Care to share a link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T21:22:48-07:00","id":1327130,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant/posts/2574076\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2574076</a><br /> <br /> It\u2019s on the comments, under a comment I made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T22:17:00-07:00","id":1327136,"title":"","content":"The bit about Mega-Speed apparently benefiting Defense is another thing that the book really should state clearly.<br /> <br /> As currently written, I would never in a million years have guessed that Mega-Speed did anything other than allow you to move from place to place faster.<br /> <br /> (I kinda wonder if Mega-Speed adding one's full Mega-Dexterity Scale bonus to Defense might be unbalancing. On the other side of things, Accuracy seems more costly for less benefit. But then, I guess there are a lot of ways to add Enhancement to attacks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T03:55:36-07:00","id":1327155,"title":"","content":"For instance as written (and others may interpret it differently), someone with Mega Presence 3 does seem any more charming on a personal level (one on one) than someone without. I feel like the various scales need to be spelled out explicitly as well the various mega attributes relation to them. I will be leaving feedback as to that later today. I guess one might argue that in the above example the Mega Presence guy would receive +6 enhancement for the scale difference, but as I said it doesn\u2019t seem clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T04:20:15-07:00","id":1327158,"title":"","content":"Agree with you, the scales were not well defined in the book, for example they don\u2019t tell that Leadership affect people on the one on one. Also they don\u2019t give examples for what is Leadership 1 to 6, 6 is the president or 4 is the president?<br /> <br /> The scales that are clear to me are Size, Power, Durability, Speed and Might (they are physical).<br /> Leadership and Mental are a bit unclear what are the benchmarks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-24-2019, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T05:05:26-07:00","id":1327164,"title":"","content":"I get the idea that they are narrative tools. (been reading up a lot on Scale and how it has been implemented). What I want is strong guidelines of how and when to use Scale so that Storyguides and players can be on the same page. The biggest anxiety with Scale right now is that at many tables there will be arguments that flare up because of what Scale applies when.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T05:21:34-07:00","id":1327165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327164#post1327164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the idea that they are narrative tools. (been reading up a lot on Scale and how it has been implemented). What I want is strong guidelines of how and when to use Scale so that Storyguides and players can be on the same page. The biggest anxiety with Scale right now is that at many tables there will be arguments that flare up because of what Scale applies when.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. That is one thing that I agree completely, there will be confusion, not in the MAtt matter, but on the \u201cdoes my size matter in this situation\u201d or \u201ccan I use my mental power to convince a mathematician because he is focused on logic and not social skills\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T05:36:37-07:00","id":1327166,"title":"","content":"I realize hedge cases and exceptions exist, this is a TTRPG after all. However, I want to decrease the back and forth and workload of the Storyguide as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T09:28:25-07:00","id":1327195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327164#post1327164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the idea that they are narrative tools. (been reading up a lot on Scale and how it has been implemented). What I want is strong guidelines of how and when to use Scale so that Storyguides and players can be on the same page. The biggest anxiety with Scale right now is that at many tables there will be arguments that flare up because of what Scale applies when.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The blog post that was copied into the KS update is pretty clear, and echos the actual text while just being more concise and precise.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">But that prompts the question: When do characters get </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">? And the answer is: when a piece of equipment or the character\u2019s powers say they do. Characters in the Trinity Continuum get </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> through powers and sometimes equipment. Talents have Gifts, psions have Psi powers, and novas have Quantum Traits that all give them some access to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, which applies in certain arenas and on specific rolls, but not all rolls. Talents can spend Inspiration to increase their </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> for a single action, hopefully reducing the difference between themselves and something bigger than them, or making them so much better than the average human that it shows as </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. Novas will have some ways to get inherent </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Scale</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> bonuses to certain actions as described in the power.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The underlying thing to remember is that Scale is both subjective (given by the Storyguide in places where it makes sense, because an item or creature deserves to narratively have Scale) and objective (given by the game book by a power or in a piece of equipment\u2019s description). This means that sometimes your character will mostly get Scale through her powers or equipment via what the game book says and sometimes when the Storyguide says, and non-player characters will always get Scale because of both when the Storyguide decides it and because the book suggested it.&quot;<br /> <br /> When powers give Scale is explicit, but SG has permission to let it apply elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> navigating KS comments is a nightmare, especially with as many as there are. Could you copy paste or screenshot? From your description it sounds like it was more of a description of how scale works in general, and not saying that Speed Scale applies to Defense directly, natively without SG writ.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T09:44:46-07:00","id":1327199,"title":"","content":"Not Mateus but let\u2019s see if I can help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz at kickstarter comments</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great explanations on the way to use scale when dealing with Nova Mega-Attributes. This part of a Nova can lift and throw was not clear on the Manuscript, but now I think I am very comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Left me with one question about when we are on the bad side of the scale:<br /> <br /> I have scale 2 Might and want to lift a scale 3 object, what\u2019s the complication?<br /> <br /> I have scale 1 speed and want to hit a Mega-Speed 2 Nova, what\u2019s the complication?<br /> <br /> I am a Psiad using my pirokinetic power to hit a Durability 3 target, how many successes I use to inflict injury?<br /> <br /> It looks like 3 questions, but you probably know it\u2019s only one...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Kenson at kickstarter comments replying to Mateus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) +2 increase in difficulty for the Athletics + Might roll.<br /> <br /> 2) +2 increase in difficulty on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> 3) +4 increase in difficulty on the attack roll. If, by &quot;Durability,&quot; you're talking about armor, that has a specific effect of increasing the successes needed for an Inflict Damage stunt.<br /> <br /> In general, a 1-level difference in Scale equals either two successes on a roll or a +2 increase in the difficulty of a roll (which is the equivalent of \u20132 successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>And for a bonus:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Danielle Lauzon responding to the same subject at kickstarter comments</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that the +2 Difficulty is a thing for player rolls. Because Antagonists work differently than characters, if they are attacking your character with less Scale, your Defensive Scale applies as an Enhancement to the roll you are making to take a Defensive Action. This is *effectively exactly the same thing* but could make a difference in some edge cases so it's worth pointing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope this helps/clears out some matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T10:08:27-07:00","id":1327203,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1629_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1629\" data-vbnamecard=\"1629\">Possessed</a>, I'll submit feedback on that then, because as written Mega-Dex and Mega-Speed do not apply to Attack or Defense rolls. Yes, you can sub attributes with SG permission, but we have other Edges and Powers that let you sub normal usage. If it was expected you could do it all the time, then why waste the wordcount?<br /> <br /> The Dramatic Scale section of Mega-Dexterity seemed like it was worded to try and be non-combat type rolls, especially since RAW you don't Close Combat attack or Defend with Dex.<br /> <br /> &quot;Increase their Dramatic Scale by their Mega-Dexterity dots when performing a Dexterity task faster than or against an opponent: 2 Enhancement per difference in Scale. In this case, the nova does not ignore Complications or reduce Difficulty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T11:16:37-07:00","id":1327211,"title":"","content":"So, looking at what is being said further, it looks like they aren't implying this is some benefit specific to Mega-Speed, but is instead part of Speed Scale in general, which would be good for Psions as that is the easiest Scale for them to get.<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by the prospect of Differences in Speed Scale applying to Attack/Defense. Also, interestingly enough, it wouldn't cancel Durability out, so if the super fast nova is attacking the super durable nova, they both get Scale.<br /> <br /> This also lead me to reread the Combat and Scale section of Core, where it specifically calls out that extra damage is only a function of Power against Durability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T11:30:00-07:00","id":1327215,"title":"","content":"The benefit of speed scale apply to psions, vehicles and animals, but only when they are running (or flying) at that speed scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T11:40:50-07:00","id":1327218,"title":"","content":"Understandable, but I'm not seeing that listed as a benefit in Core or anywhere else. I'm seeing where speed scale gives you extra rangebands of movement, and how it applies to chases, but nothing for Attack/Defense.<br /> <br /> I'm with you on the theory, it definitely seems like something it should do, I'm just looking for the text support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T12:04:28-07:00","id":1327223,"title":"","content":"Core use Scale on a loose way, even on Aeon there is little use of scale described. Aberrant is supposed to be the one dealing with scale all the time.<br /> <br /> Talents for example can raise one scale to any action by spending one inspiration, but there is no comment of what it means exactly.<br /> <br /> Even Scion have a lose way to deal with it, you gain a scale, good add +2 enhancements on related actions.<br /> <br /> The idea for scale, and basically for the entire Storypath system, is to deal with it narratively, with just enough rules to start playing with no need to check the book all the time, yet having a good rule structure to add what is needed on a easy way and without breaking everything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T12:21:21-07:00","id":1327227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327223#post1327223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea for scale, and basically for the entire Storypath system, is to deal with it narratively, with just enough rules to start playing with no need to check the book all the time, yet having a good rule structure to add what is needed on a easy way and without breaking everything</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the real key to Scale is to apply it when it makes sense. Does a Mega-Speed nova get Scale to defense? Sure, if their speed works in a way which lets them dodge quickly. But I would argue that an attacker with Mega-Cunning could oppose that Scale with their extremely quick reactions or ability to predict that the speedster will be in exactly the spot they're punching at. I know people want to avoid SG calls, but Storypath kind of relies on that, or at least on table-wide calls. I like to use the &quot;You've got to be kidding me!&quot; rule. If someone says, &quot;I think I should be able to apply my Scale here,&quot; and no one says, &quot;You've got to be kidding me,&quot; then it applies. Error on the side of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T12:44:52-07:00","id":1327232,"title":"","content":"Let's see if I can break this down quickly, based on what has been said. When I mention &quot;Counters&quot; I mean that each point of Scale removes a point of Scale from the opponent. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Durability </b>- Scale used to determine how physically tough and hardy the Nova is. This counters instance of the Might and Power Scale. If a nova's Durability is higher than the attacker's Scale then increase the nova's Soft Armor by +2 per difference in Scale. <br /> <br /> <b>Leadership </b>- The overall social magnetism and acumen the Nova possess when dealing with others. This scale counters and is countered by the Leadership Scale of others. <br /> <br /> <b>Might </b>- The physical power of the Nova and how much force they can exert. This only counters other Might Scales when in a contest of strength, and is countered by an enemies' Durability Scale when attacking with their Might Scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental </b>- A nova's capabilities in the arena of the mind. A nova's Mental Scale counters and is countered by another creature's Mental Scale. <br /> <br /> <b>Power </b>- The raw quantum potency of a Nova's various abilities. Mostly used for Range quantum attacks. This counters other Powers scales if there is a direct conflict. It is countered by Speed or Durability when attacking. <br /> <br /> <b>Size </b>- The physical size in relation to everything else around them. Rarely does it directly interact with other Size Scales, likely that it will augment other types of Scales. IE Might, Durability, and even Speed Scales.<br /> <br /> <b>Speed </b>- How fast the Nova can move and react. This can be used when attacking, similar to Might Scale. It counters Speed Scales. When used when defending the nova gains +2 Enhancement to their Defensive Rolls per point of Scale Difference. <br /> <br /> If Scales are used against others that do not directly Counter each other, IE a Mega-Might Nova punches a Mega-Speed Nova. They would both compare their respective Scales, Attacker's Might -&gt; Defender Durability, and Defenders Speed -&gt; Attacker's Speed. And they would add their respective enhancements from Scale to their various rolls. <br /> <br /> <br /> Is my thinking right? Close? What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T13:01:57-07:00","id":1327237,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand, you did a great job here.<br /> <br /> Like the explanation on Might x Speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T13:12:14-07:00","id":1327239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327227#post1327227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the real key to Scale is to apply it when it makes sense. Does a Mega-Speed nova get Scale to defense? Sure, if their speed works in a way which lets them dodge quickly. But I would argue that an attacker with Mega-Cunning could oppose that Scale with their extremely quick reactions or ability to predict that the speedster will be in exactly the spot they're punching at. I know people want to avoid SG calls, but Storypath kind of relies on that, or at least on table-wide calls. I like to use the &amp;quot;You've got to be kidding me!&amp;quot; rule. If someone says, &amp;quot;I think I should be able to apply my Scale here,&amp;quot; and no one says, &amp;quot;You've got to be kidding me,&amp;quot; then it applies. Error on the side of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That &quot;You've got to be kidding me!&quot; rule is great, it is a lot like the \u201cOuch\u201d rule for Wraith, it\u2019s fun and works.<br /> GMing D&amp;D for years, I am really happy with not needing to go thru a book for a rule (I actually improvised half of the game just because it was annoying as hell go thru 50 pages of spells).<br /> Of course it\u2019s not for beginners, SGs may need to have some previous experience with other more rules heavy games, or played more than a few sessions using the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T14:47:09-07:00","id":1327264,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it has a flexibility, and expectation for you to play fast and loose, rule of cool/fun, but there is still an objective baseline set of assumptions and rules. They aren't totally binding, but they are there. It is really all in that blog post.<br /> <br /> If the SG is having to award subjective scale for every action of your power, there really should be an objective rule.<br /> <br /> Again, I like the prospect of this ruling, but I'm also curious how this shakes out against the rest of the prescribed parts of the system.<br /> <br /> I know that a common sense SG could rule this applicability, but especially in a new system there should be some guidance to help new SGs that don't necessarily have gut sense of what to allow. Do you need to move at your full speed to get your scale? If you moved your full allotment of range bands and ended your turn in Close range and attacked someone, would you still get your Speed Scale bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:31:59-07:00","id":1327285,"title":"","content":"What about the Mega-Fast Punch, in the Infinite Mass Punch from flash? Can you add Speed scale on the attack?<br /> <br /> I personally would put this as an Power Stunt, requiring one quantum point per scale at least and possibly an action or two to get far away enough and run back to hit on maximum speed. Finally, I would put a complication that would hurt the speedster when attacking unless bought off.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s one thing that come into my mind when I was reading again the power stunt text. It\u2019s fascinating how we can play with it with out breaking the rules... not much at least...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:08:08-07:00","id":1327313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327285#post1327285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Mega-Fast Punch, in the Infinite Mass Punch from flash? Can you add Speed scale on the attack?<br /> <br /> I personally would put this as an Power Stunt, requiring one quantum point per scale at least and possibly an action or two to get far away enough and run back to hit on maximum speed. Finally, I would put a complication that would hurt the speedster when attacking unless bought off.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s one thing that come into my mind when I was reading again the power stunt text. It\u2019s fascinating how we can play with it with out breaking the rules... not much at least...</div> </div> </div> </div>Power stunt works, easiest way though would be to make it a melee quantum attack with a negative tag &quot;only while running&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:29:46-07:00","id":1327321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327313#post1327313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Power stunt works, easiest way though would be to make it a melee quantum attack with a negative tag &amp;quot;only while running&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, much better.<br /> <br /> The idea was more about \u201cok, if you want to try it, that\u2019s what you gonna do\u201d, once the Nova do it a few more times or want to be able to do that easily, learn the power properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:14:21-07:00","id":1327400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327285#post1327285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Mega-Fast Punch, in the Infinite Mass Punch from flash? Can you add Speed scale on the attack?<br /> <br /> I personally would put this as an Power Stunt, requiring one quantum point per scale at least and possibly an action or two to get far away enough and run back to hit on maximum speed. Finally, I would put a complication that would hurt the speedster when attacking unless bought off.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s one thing that come into my mind when I was reading again the power stunt text. It\u2019s fascinating how we can play with it with out breaking the rules... not much at least...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that basically the Rapid Strike Mega-Edge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:20:42-07:00","id":1327403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327400#post1327400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that basically the Rapid Strike Mega-Edge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rapid Strike is about hitting several times, my suggestion is about a super speed charge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=By7wTrI3ZJ0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=By7wTrI3ZJ0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=By7wTrI3ZJ0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=By7wTrI3ZJ0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> When he was running to hit it was the idea, when he is about to finish it\u2019s the Rapid Strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-25-2019, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:51:41-07:00","id":1327409,"title":"","content":"This is perhaps a bit clearer example of what you mean <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=GuHmVqgy_5U\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=GuHmVqgy_5U\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=GuHmVqgy_5U\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=GuHmVqgy_5U </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So not the Rapid Strike but a singular hit that scales up from what the speedster is usually capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:05:35-07:00","id":1327411,"title":"","content":"Sure, but the effect of Rapid Strike is to add enhancements equal to either your Mega-Dex or Mega-Cunning for 1 quantum. Why not just re-skin it to Super Sonic Punch? Or, if since you have to have Mega-Speed as a prerequisite, add it as scale instead of enhancements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T17:31:53-07:00","id":1327669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1326813#post1326813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I goofed. It is CC AND Dex for the Precise Martial Arts Edges, so there is a precedent for Edges allowing Dex to contribute to Defense.<br /> <br /> So we have some precedent, and then there is the Mega-Edge Rapid Strike that boosts Attacks, so I think there is a case for it. But it shouldn't be Scale, or at least 1 to 1 Scale. MMight giving combat scale always on for no cost is kinda warping. Still working through how that shakes down, and also really makes me question if MStam is supposed to actually work as defensive Scale, or if that was a holdover in the MMight entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do the Precise Martial Arts edges let you base your defense off dexterity? I can\u2019t find it in the Trinity Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T17:35:54-07:00","id":1327671,"title":"","content":"It requires dexterity and add a enhancement, but don\u2019t use dexterity properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T17:16:06-07:00","id":1327816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1326765-aberrant-super-speed-defense?p=1327669#post1327669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do the Precise Martial Arts edges let you base your defense off dexterity? I can\u2019t find it in the Trinity Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't let you sub, just a way for Dex to contribute to defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}